content.text:
Landscape start sheet is cut off at bottom (fine text and claim button not visible) but scrollable. The primary button visible. Good enough. But there's no visible scroll indicator; user might not know claim button exists below. Could reduce sheet padding or make scroll. Not critical, but "finish" quality could improve by making start sheet more compact in short viewports via media query. Add:
```
@media(max-height:520px){
 .sheet{padding:14px 16px 12px}
 .logo{font-size:1.5rem}
 .tagline{margin-top:4px;font-size:.7rem}
 .prize{margin-top:8px;padding:6px 9px;font-size:.7rem}
 .how{margin-top:8px;gap:5px}
 .how div{padding:6px}
 .how span{font-size:.6rem}
 .primary{margin-top:9px;padding:10px}
 .secondary{margin-top:6px;padding:8px}
 .fine{margin-top:6px}
}
```
This will fit landscape likely. Also for very short mobile. Let's add.

Also gameplay landscape screenshot check.

